        "abstract": "High voltage alternating current gas insulated systems are utilized in narrow spaces. In operation electric field peaks can occur and may impair the functioning of the system. The knowledge of the electric field distribution in gas insulated lines is essential to ensure a reliable operation of the system. This can be determined by numerical simulations and requires a fast linear solver. Utilizing the AmgX library on NVIDIA graphic processing units allows a fast solution of a Poisson system of linear equations with millions of degrees of freedom within fractions of a second.",
